   "id": "leverage_basics",
   "title": "What leverage does to your money",
   "body": "Leverage means a position is bigger than the money you put in. Just arithmetic: if a position ten times the size of your ₹40,000 falls by 10%, that is a loss equal to your whole ₹40,000. SEBI's risk disclosure document says that in derivatives you may lose part or all of the margin, and the loss may exceed the original margin amount. This is about size, not a forecast about prices.",
